From: pdx203 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: gpu: name a re-import by the pages it pins

The import sample (0024) calls an import "again" when the same address and size came in the last 64 imports, but a read-only view
or a new surface can be given an address a freed one had. Each import now records its first physical page; GPUIMPORT says whether
the process imported the same pages (same size) in its last 256 imports and how long before, or none of them had them (a new
surface), with running counts of each.

